WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:05.027
Small airway reopening can produce rapid fluid stresses. Direct

00:00:05.027 --> 00:00:09.504
observation inside a whole lung is difficult to standardise.

00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:19.110
A parallel-plate flow chamber permits controlled fluid motion over

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:23.545
a monolayer. This simplified geometry is a modelling decision.

00:00:28.675 --> 00:00:32.523
The published method uses a flow-induced stress event

00:00:32.523 --> 00:00:36.372
to study damage to cells under controlled exposure conditions.

00:00:40.967 --> 00:00:45.538
Fluorescence-based injury measurements must be timed, controlled and interpreted

00:00:45.538 --> 00:00:50.110
with care. A signal is not a complete injury mechanism.

00:00:55.383 --> 00:01:00.051
The chamber isolates a mechanical challenge. It does not recreate

00:01:00.051 --> 00:01:04.718
airway anatomy, immune dynamics or every interaction in a human lung.

00:01:10.092 --> 00:01:14.679
A reproducible instrument turns an invisible question into a

00:01:14.679 --> 00:01:19.267
measurable experiment. The paper records its operating logic and limits.
